---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import ContactEmail from '../../components/ContactEmail.astro';
import { LEGAL_ENTITY, LEGAL_ADDRESS } from '../../config';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<Legal
  lang={lang}
  path="/privacy"
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  title="Privacy Policy · Hydravia"
  description="How Hydravia handles your data: local history, location for weather, subscriptions. No account, no trackers."
>
  <p>
    Hydravia is built to work without an account and without a server. Almost
    everything stays on your phone. This page sets out exactly what stays local, the
    few cases where something is sent to a third party, and why.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    The app is published by <span class="todo">{LEGAL_ENTITY}</span>, at
    <span class="todo">{LEGAL_ADDRESS}</span>. For any question about your data,
    write to <ContactEmail />.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What stays on your phone</h2>
  <p>
    The following is stored in a local database on your device only. It is never
    transmitted to us and never backed up to our servers, for the simple reason
    that we do not run any.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Your weight</strong>, used to compute your daily goal.</li>
    <li><strong>Your active hours</strong> (wake, sleep) and your reminder interval.</li>
    <li><strong>Your intake history</strong>: every amount, with its date and time.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your preferences</strong>: whether reminders are on, which apps you
      selected for the lock.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can erase your intake history at any time from
    <strong>Settings → Data → Delete history</strong>. Deletion is immediate and
    permanent. Uninstalling the app removes all of this data, settings included.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Location and weather</h2>
  <p>
    If you grant location access (only while using the app), and only in that case,
    Hydravia reads your location to look up the outside temperature, which slightly
    adjusts the recommended dose in hot weather. The coordinates are rounded to about
    1 km before anything is sent.
  </p>
  <p>
    Those rounded coordinates are sent to <strong>Open-Meteo</strong>
    (<a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/terms" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">open-meteo.com</a>),
    a weather service that requires no API key and ties the request to no profile.
    As with any internet connection, Open-Meteo also receives your device's IP
    address.
    Hydravia does not retain your location: it is used for the request, and only the
    resulting temperature is held in memory for 30 minutes.
  </p>
  <p>
    If you decline the permission, the app works normally: dose calculation simply
    ignores the weather.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Screen Time and app blocking</h2>
  <p>
    On iOS the lock is built on <strong>Screen Time</strong> (Apple's
    <em>Family Controls</em> framework). Apple deliberately keeps this API sandboxed:
    it lets Hydravia apply a block to apps <strong>you select yourself</strong>,
    without ever granting access to your usage statistics.
  </p>
  <p>
    In practice, <strong>Hydravia cannot see</strong> which apps you use, or for how
    long. Your selection stays on your device, inside a system-managed container. You
    can revoke this permission at any time in
    <strong>iOS Settings → Screen Time</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Subscriptions</h2>
  <p>
    Payments are handled by <strong>Apple</strong>. We never see your payment details.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your subscription status is checked directly with the App Store, on your device.
    No receipt, no identifier and none of your hydration data is sent to us.
  </p>

  <h2>6. What we do not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No user account, so no email address or password is collected.</li>
    <li>No advertising trackers and no behavioural analytics SDK.</li>
    <li>No selling or sharing of data for commercial purposes.</li>
    <li>No advertising profiling and no cross-app tracking.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Recipients at a glance</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Recipient</th>
        <th>Data sent</th>
        <th>When</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Open-Meteo</td>
        <td>Rounded coordinates (~1 km), IP address</td>
        <td>Only if you allow location access</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Apple</td>
        <td>Payment and subscription data</td>
        <td>Only when purchasing or restoring</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the GDPR you have rights of access, rectification, erasure, restriction and
    portability over your personal data. Because Hydravia holds no database about
    you, most of these rights are exercised directly on your phone: your data is on
    your device, and you can view or delete it whenever you want.
  </p>
  <p>
    For any request about your data, write to
    <ContactEmail />. You also have the right
    to lodge a complaint with the data protection authority in your country.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Children</h2>
  <p>
    Hydravia is not directed at children under 13 and does not knowingly collect
    their data.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This policy may change as the app evolves. The last updated date appears at the
    top of this page; for any significant change we will say so in the app.
  </p>
</Legal>
